Bug 2076034 - Stop extractHeaderAddressMailboxes from truncating non-Latin-1 characters. r=jtracey

nsIMsgHeaderParser.extractHeaderAddressMailboxes was declared with
ACString, so XPConnect narrowed the already decoded header value to
Latin-1 by keeping only the low byte of each character. The JS
implementation then parsed that mangled string. U+0269 became "i", so
alɩce@example.com was extracted as alice@example.com. U+200B and most
other Unicode spaces became control characters that the parser dropped.

Declare the method with AString so the value reaches the parser intact.

Added test cases to test_nsIMsgHeaderParser2.js for a Unicode letter
and a quoted U+200B local part.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329718


diff --git a/mailnews/mime/public/nsIMsgHeaderParser.idl b/mailnews/mime/public/nsIMsgHeaderParser.idl
--- a/mailnews/mime/public/nsIMsgHeaderParser.idl
+++ b/mailnews/mime/public/nsIMsgHeaderParser.idl
@@ -177,16 +177,16 @@ interface nsIMsgHeaderParser : nsISuppor
   /**
    * Given a string which contains a list of Header addresses, returns a
    * comma-separated list of just the `mailbox' portions.
    *
    * @param aLine          The header line to parse.
    * @return               A comma-separated list of just the mailbox parts
    *                       of the email-addresses.
    */
-  ACString extractHeaderAddressMailboxes(in ACString aLine);
+  AString extractHeaderAddressMailboxes(in AString aLine);
 
   /**
    * Given a name and email address, produce a string that is suitable for
    * emitting in a MIME header (after applying RFC 2047 encoding).
    */
   AString makeMimeAddress(in AString aName, in AString aEmail);
 };
diff --git a/mailnews/mime/test/unit/test_nsIMsgHeaderParser2.js b/mailnews/mime/test/unit/test_nsIMsgHeaderParser2.js
--- a/mailnews/mime/test/unit/test_nsIMsgHeaderParser2.js
+++ b/mailnews/mime/test/unit/test_nsIMsgHeaderParser2.js
@@ -60,16 +60,29 @@ function run_test() {
     ],
